					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1922529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609254273" alt="Agent MacLeod" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1922529)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;" >Agent MacLeod</a></span> <span class="odate time_1411867935 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Sep 2014 01:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2120026">
									

<p>I'm not sure why I upvoted. The comedy isn't hitting me very hard, and neither is the horror. It reminds me of <a href="/scp-2222">SCP-2222</a> in its cold treatment of human beings, and of <a href="http://www.goominet.com/unspeakable-vault/">the Unspeakable Vault of Doom</a> in its absurdity. However, this doesn't have nearly as much meat on its bones as the two things I linked. Still, I'm leaving the upvote because it could just be that I'm tired.<br />
Edit: Now that I've read the forum post that lead to the creation of this, I'm far more amused. My +1 is now enthusiastic.</p>
<p>Edit 2: Changing to downvote. This is more like an Extranormal event than an SCP. Oh, some alien made a phone call that breaks logic and causality? Big fuckin deal, 682 just breached containment and killed a dozen employees, the DEER has decided we're not giving it enough sacrifices, and the deal with the CotBG involving 2217 just went sour, plus some dumb bastard let 447-2 touch a dead body. This wouldn't even register on the Foundation's radar unless Human Mills were located and it turns out they're mass-producing philosophical zombies and selling them in bulk to extraterrestrials. <strong>THAT</strong> would warrant SCP classification while still allowing room for the original idea to hang out in the article</p>

